==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/maɪˈtoʊsɪs/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|əʊsɪs|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|de|en}} {{m|de|Mitosis}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|μίτος||thread}} + {{m|de|-osis}}, probably in reference to the thread-like [[chromatin]] seen during mitosis.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|mitoses}}

# {{lb|en|cytology}} The [[division]] of a cell [[nucleus]] in which the [[genome]] is copied and separated into two identical halves. It is normally followed by cell division.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|karyokinesis}}

====Meronyms====
* {{l|en|prophase}}
* {{l|en|metaphase}}
* {{l|en|anaphase}}
* {{l|en|telophase}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|mitotic}}
* {{l|en|mitotically}}

====See also====
* {{l|en|meiosis}}

